464 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /H3
/T (            At TechPlusSolutions, I gained hands-on experience across the entire application development life cycle, from requirements gathering and sprint planning to deployment and maintenance. I applied Agile methodologies with iterative development and sprint cycles, becoming familiar with the flow of real-world production environments.            I  worked extensively on Flutter project structures, organizing code using feature-based and layer-based approaches for better scalability. I implemented robust design architecture using MVVM and Clean Architecture principles, while managing app state with tools like Provider, Riverpod, and GetX. My work emphasized code separation, dependency injection, and testability for long-term maintainability.         In collaboration with the team, I used Git for version control and participated in pull requests and branching strategies. I regularly worked with GitHub, Jira, and Slack for task tracking and communication. For debugging and error handling, I utilized Flutter DevTools, Crashlytics, and implemented user-friendly error reporting using try-catch and custom handlers.         My responsibilities included state management, widget tree optimization, and performance tuning through rebuild minimization and integration testing. I planned navigation flows and UI state using Figma/Adobe XD and contributed to testing strategies and bug fixing during the QA phase. I implemented REST API integration using Dio, managed data persistence with SQLite and SharedPreferences, and configured App Store/Google Play deployment.               Lastly, I handled package management using pubspec.yaml, integrating dependencies like Dio, GetX, and intl. My contributions covered cross-platform app development, targeting both Android and iOS, giving me a strong foundation in scalable Flutter development.)
/E (            At TechPlusSolutions, I gained hands-on experience across the entire application development life cycle, from requirements gathering and sprint planning to deployment and maintenance. I applied Agile methodologies with iterative development and sprint cycles, becoming familiar with the flow of real-world production environments.            I  worked extensively on Flutter project structures, organizing code using feature-based and layer-based approaches for better scalability. I implemented robust design architecture using MVVM and Clean Architecture principles, while managing app state with tools like Provider, Riverpod, and GetX. My work emphasized code separation, dependency injection, and testability for long-term maintainability.         In collaboration with the team, I used Git for version control and participated in pull requests and branching strategies. I regularly worked with GitHub, Jira, and Slack for task tracking and communication. For debugging and error handling, I utilized Flutter DevTools, Crashlytics, and implemented user-friendly error reporting using try-catch and custom handlers.         My responsibilities included state management, widget tree optimization, and performance tuning through rebuild minimization and integration testing. I planned navigation flows and UI state using Figma/Adobe XD and contributed to testing strategies and bug fixing during the QA phase. I implemented REST API integration using Dio, managed data persistence with SQLite and SharedPreferences, and configured App Store/Google Play deployment.               Lastly, I handled package management using pubspec.yaml, integrating dependencies like Dio, GetX, and intl. My contributions covered cross-platform app development, targeting both Android and iOS, giving me a strong foundation in scalable Flutter development.)
/Pg 16 0 R
/K [19 20]
>>
endobj
